==Battleground==
*1 [[Mooth]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Mooth]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*2 [[Zollow]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Zollow]]s spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**4 [[Zollow]]s spawn, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
First, wait out the two Mooths and two Zollows, then kill them. Make sure that you use the money from the Mooths wisely, as you'll have a lot of it. Once you have a lot of money, hit the base and release M. Ost. Use your usual methods of killing him, with [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] cats such as [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] and [[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Catman]], or any strong generalist [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]]/[[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythics]], like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] or [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]]. The Zollows appear pretty infrequently, but they have the potential to wipe out all of your anti-Relic cats in one hit. When that happens, just keep meatshielding and spawn more, repeating this until M. Ost is dead.

==Trivia==
*This stage's name may be a reference to the [[wikia:Mario:Dry Bones|Dry Bones]] enemies from the ''[[wikipedia:Mario (franchise)|Mario]]'' franchise, as sodden is an antonym of dry and Zollow's collapsing and reassembling animations are quite similar to the Dry Bones' own.

